preConditionHook:
// GRIMES'S NAMED BREAKOUT BASE: a tight recent range sitting at the TOP of a
// much larger range (long) / at its bottom (short) -- "a small range near a
// resistance level ... is referred to as a breakout base", the coil that
// builds the energy for the break.
//
// TWO TERMS, both on NESTED current-inclusive windows:
//   * SIZE -- the tight window's height is at most tightFraction of the big
//     window's height (25 percent is the book's own figure);
//   * POSITION -- the tight window's own top sits within proximityFraction of
//     the big window's top, so the coil is at the far end of the range and not
//     in its middle. proximityFraction is a guess and is meant to be
//     optimized; at a large enough value the position term is inert and the
//     rule is the size term alone.
//
// WRITTEN AS MULTIPLICATIONS, never as a ratio: a zero-height outer range is
// legal data and EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero.
//
// Not RangeWidthBelowAtrMultiple (merge decision 8), which sizes ONE window
// against ATR and has no position term at all. Not ShrinkingConsecutiveRanges,
// which compares two ADJACENT EQUAL-LENGTH windows rather than a nested pair.
// Not CloseInRangePosition, which places the closing price inside the big
// range where this places the tight window's own EDGE. Not TightChannel, net progress plus
// pullback depth. The rule being mirrored, neither half is reachable from the
// other side's placement.
//
// Every comparison is a difference against a difference, so the rule passes
// the shift test; no ATR and no state.
//
// The window loops mirror EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest()
// call: seeded at the window's first bar, scanning the rest, strict comparison
// under the EL relational tolerance -- hence el_gt / el_lt, as in Breakout.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(tightLookback, rangeLookback) - 1.
tightHigh = high[0];
tightLow = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)tightLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], tightHigh)) tightHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], tightLow)) tightLow = low[i];
}
rangeHigh = high[0];
rangeLow = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], rangeHigh)) rangeHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], rangeLow)) rangeLow = low[i];
}
